      {
        "pageid": 5820909,
        "ns": 0,
        "title": "There Will Come Soft Rains (short story)",
        "extract": "\"There Will Come Soft Rains\"  is a science fiction short story by author Ray Bradbury  written as a chronicle about a lone house that stands intact in a California city that has otherwise been obliterated by a nuclear bomb. The title is from a 1918 poem of the same name by Sara Teasdale that was published during World War I and the Spanish flu pandemic. The story was first published in 1950 in two different versions in two separate publications, a one-page short story in Collier's magazine and a chapter of the fix-up  novel The Martian Chronicles.\nThe author regarded it as \"the one story that represents the essence of Ray Bradbury\". Bradbury's...",
